  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "This private compatibility module only declares the legacy resource and\n selector address shapes; it has no handwritten executable code. Its derived\n serialization and identity operations do not emit source-line measurements.\n The source-tool argument and delivery regressions in `agent/tests.rs`\n exercise these addresses through the legacy adapter. Supported path-based\n address construction is tested separately in `tests/outline_content.rs`."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/src/resource.rs` (file root) is acceptable.\n\n- **No handwritten code.** The file contains only `struct[ResourceId]` and `struct[OutlineId]`. Both are plain field declarations with `#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Serialize, Deserialize)]`, and there are no functions. This matches the commentary that the module only declares address shapes and that its derived operations produce no source-line measurements.\n- **Private compatibility module.** `lib.rs` declares it as `mod resource;`, which is private. `OutlineId` is `#[cfg(test)]`, which fits the \"legacy\" description.\n- **Regressions in `agent/tests.rs` exist.** These tests build and use `ResourceId` values: `source_reads_track_optional_dependencies_and_empty_searches_remain_discovery`, `source_outlines_present_every_top_level_and_nested_item`, and the `SourceProvider` test impls. `agent/sources.rs#dispatch` deserializes `ResourceId` from tool arguments, and `agent.rs` uses `OutlineId` in the `SourceTools` `ToolFactory` impl. So the source-tool argument and delivery paths exercise these addresses through the legacy adapter.\n- **Path-based construction is tested separately.** `tests/outline_content.rs#fn[addresses_reconstruct_without_reading_the_file]` tests path-based `OutlineData` address construction, serialization round-trip and hashing. This supports the last sentence of the commentary.\n\nThe explanation is substantive rather than just citing difficulty. It agrees with the current source, and the citation is on the file root, which is where a file-threshold exception belongs. I found no gap.",
